After it was revealed that Robert Pattinson was tapped as the next 007 , fellow industry notables are speaking out to congratulate him on the casting.

On Monday, it was announced that Pattinson would be taking over the iconic James Bond role from Daniel Craig, who concluded his run with 2021's No Time to Die . He'll star in the upcoming film from director Denis Villeneuve.

"I am overjoyed to welcome Robert Pattinson as our new James Bond . He has the timeless soul of 007 and brings a spirit that is completely new. I cannot wait to begin,&#8221; the filmmaker said in a statement. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies We Now Know What Robert Pattinson Was Doing When the James Bond Casting News Broke Movies Robert Pattinson Manifested His James Bond Casting 14 Years Ago

Some of Pattinson's former co-stars, such as Florence Pugh ( Dune: Part Three ), Elizabeth Debicki ( Tenet ), Bryce Dallas Howard ( The Twilight Saga: Eclipse ), Ralph Fiennes ( Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire ) and Rami Malek ( The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn &#8211; Part 2 ), and fellow celebrities, including Brad Pitt and Joseph Zada, are among those reacting to the news.

"I'm so happy because he's been the no. 1 vote in my household for like quite a long time," Pugh told The Hollywood Reporter at Elle's Women in Hollywood celebration. "He's so unbelievably talented. He makes moves that you're just not guessing, and it's just so wonderful to see a career just float and be this unbelievably versatile thing. I'm so excited that he got that role. So good, and with Denis."

Speaking with E! News , Howard praised her time working with Pattinson, saying, "He's not schmoozy. He's not trying to be cool. He's just who he is, and he happens to be absolutely gorgeous. But he's a true artist, and his career since Twilight has obviously demonstrated that a zillion times over." So for her, &#8220;Him as James Bond feels really right&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Fiennes, who also appeared in three previous Bond films, learned about Pattinson's casting during an interview with Andy Cohen on his SiriusXM show, alongside The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping castmembers. &#8220;I'm sorry. I'm in love with Daniel Craig still," he said. &#8220;It's hard. I've got the wrench in my heart." However, Fiennes later clarified that he believes the Twilight alum is &#8220;a great actor,&#8221; adding, &#8220;I'm sure he'll be great.&#8221;

Debicki told Variety she's &#8220;so happy for Rob&#8221; at the Los Angeles premiere of The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth . &#8220;He is an enigma himself. He's beautiful, and he's funny, and he's smart&#x2026; I think he's perfect. I'm so thrilled,&#8221; she added of his casting.

Pitt appeared shocked when ExtraTV broke the Bond news to him at the The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth premiere. &#8220;Is that right?!&#8221; he replied. &#8220;You know what? I love this idea. I love what he's been doing; I love his choices. I think he's the real deal. Yeah, that's great. Good call; I like it.&#8221;

Malek told People that he &#8220;could not be more proud&#8221; of Pattinson, having &#8220;known Rob for quite some time.&#8221; He added, &#8220;I mean, the fact that people are recognizing, maybe they all know, how talented that man is. I've known him for years. We've worked together and we've become quite close friends and it's been lovely to just share this moment with him.&#8221;

Sunrise on the Reaping star Zada also told Cohen, &#8220;He's on such a roll,&#8221; referring to his stacked lineup of projects this year &#x2014; The Drama , The Odyssey , Primetime and Dune: Part Three &#x2014; and now his Bond casting. &#8220;He's every young actor's favorite actor right now,&#8221; he added. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

A three-judge panel at the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit peppered a Nexstar Media Group lawyer with questions about the company's efforts to salvage its contested acquisition of rival Tegna.

Pay-TV operator DirecTV and attorneys general of 13 states sued last March to block the $6.2 billion transaction, which would create a local TV station behemoth with reach to some 80% of U.S. households. The day after the suit was filed, the FCC approved the merger and Nexstar swiftly declared it closed.

Just as the companies were starting to integrate, however, a federal judge granted the lawsuit plaintiffs' request for a temporary restraining order, freezing the deal pending a trial. While Tegna shareholders were paid out and the company's stock ceased trading, the company's Virginia-based operations have been kept separate from Nexstar's Texas-based footprint pending the outcome of the suit. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Channel 4 Boss Says "We Cannot Apologize Enough" To Russell Brand Victim Whose Complaint Was Twice Not Dealt With By Broadcaster News David Walliams Being Investigated By Police

Nexstar lawyer Deanne Maynard sought to lay out the company's view that the TRO should only apply to stations in 31 markets where the two companies both own stations. She asserted that the plaintiffs accepted that reduced scope in legal briefs filed during the appeal. Numerous times as she was starting to make her point, though, she was frequently interrupted by federal judges Marsha Berzon, Johnnie Rawlinson and Xavier Rodriguez during the proceeding in a Pasadena, CA courtroom. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

&#8220;In this broadcast merger context,&#8221; Maynard argued, &#8220;it's very common to hold separate stations. Across Democratic and Republican administrations, the federal DOJ has challenged mergers making very similar claims to the ones that plaintiffs make here.&#8221;

The judges all voiced skepticism that there was a clear playbook to reduce the number of stations to be held separate to just 31, rather than just blocking the entire deal, as the TRO did. &#8220;My major concern here is that we're an appellate court,&#8221; Berzon said. &#8220;The district court is there, he's considered what's feasible and what isn't, and for us to start redoing that, we'd have to have a very high confidence that there was a feasible alternative.&#8221; She later interjected, &#8220;This is a discrete kind of issue which requires an understanding of a large, integrated organization and how it can function.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Rodriguez raised the possibility that the appellate court could remand the matter to the district court. &#8220;Why do we have to decide anything now?&#8221;

That question hung in the air as attorneys for DirecTV and the states stated their case. Emily Curran of the California Department of Justice, said focusing on 31 stations rather than the full Tegna portfolio &#8220;is not a coherent proposal.&#8221; In the lower-court proceedings, she said, &#8220;We presented evidence that a full unwinding of the merger, such that the previous version of Tegna would be fully restored, would restore that lost competition, for the simple reason that the day before the merger, it was competing. And it was competing as a integrated entity that was a successful company.&#8221;

Ben Horwich of DirecTV said the plaintiffs &#8220;challenged the transaction that they put together.&#8221; It is not the job of the plaintiffs, or the court, he added, &#8220;to figure out how to achieve their business objectives by fashioning some other transaction.&#8221;

While Maynard referred to the process of narrowing down the scope of the TRO as routine, Horwich countered that the question of antitrust harm raised in merger reviews has doomed some multi-billion-dollar deals. Sinclair's attempts to merge with Tribune, and Tegna's thwarted combination with private equity firm Standard General &#8220;couldn't go forward, because there were these concerns.&#8221;

In the case of Nexstar-Tegna, he added, the notion of a subset of Tegna being kept separate as a quasi-subsidiary pending the outcome of the suit doesn't fit with Nexstar's M&A strategy. Already, eight agonizing months have passed without the usual post-merger focus on synergies and efficiencies, with Nexstar stock slipping 10% during the legal limbo period.

&#8220;It is the defendant's own business thesis that you need to be at least a certain size to cut it in this industry,&#8221; Horwich said. &#8220;To be successful, to be competitive.&#8221; Carving out 31 stations, he said, would be tantamount to &#8220;creating a bunch of orphan stations, and then trying to find homes for them. That's not what we're aiming for here. We want the competition we had before the illegal hardship.&#8221;

After the oral arguments, the judges took the case under advisement and will now work on arriving at a decision, which is expected sometime in the early part of 2027. If the panel rules against Nexstar, the company could request an en banc hearing or appeal the matter to the U.S. Supreme Court.

Meanwhile, a jury trial of the lawsuit has been scheduled for next July in the U.S. District Court for the Eastern District of California.

